IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa15-nouns`
IMPORT `coa15-ch1`
IMPORT `coa15-ch6`

-- coa15-ch4.l4: Part 18, Chapter 4 (Purchase of own shares), ss 690 to 708 (lines 9081-9319 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat. It imports coa15-ch1.l4 (the statement-of-capital check of s 663(3)) and coa15-ch6.l4
-- (s 724(1), which ss 706 and 708 ask). Reading a result: as in coa15-ch1.l4.
--
-- The text prints "a . . . resolution" in ss 694(2), (4), 697(2), (3) and 700(2), (3): a word was omitted by an amendment and the plain-text
-- rendering shows the gap. The text does not say which kind of resolution the section now asks for, so those functions take plain facts
-- ("authorised by a resolution of the company") and do not name ordinary or special (NOTES.md, finding).

DECLARE `s 691(2) act in Chapter 4` IS ONE OF
    `s 691(2) pay for the shares on purchase`
    `s 696(2) make a copy of the contract, or a memorandum of its terms, available to members`
    `s 702(2) keep a copy of the contract, or a memorandum of its terms, available for inspection`
    `s 702(5) give notice to the registrar of the place at which the copy or memorandum is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place`
    `s 707(1) deliver a return to the registrar of the purchase of shares`
    `s 708(1) give notice of cancellation to the registrar, specifying the shares cancelled`

-- ---- s 690: power of a limited company to purchase own shares ---------------------------------------------

-- src:9084 | (1) A limited company having a share capital may purchase its own shares (including any redeemable shares), subject to—
-- src:9085 | (a) the following provisions of this Chapter, and
-- src:9086 | (b) any restriction or prohibition in the company's articles.
@ref s 690(1) A limited company having a share capital may purchase its own shares, subject to this Chapter and its articles (src:9084-9086)
GIVEN `the company is a limited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles restrict or prohibit the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 690(1) the limited company may purchase its own shares` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-690-1: "may purchase its own shares, subject to ... any restriction or prohibition in the company's articles" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no); the articles-restrict branch is the one that flips
    IF (NOT `the company is a limited company having a share capital`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A limited company having a share capital may purchase its own shares"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles restrict or prohibit the purchase`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to— (b) any restriction or prohibition in the company's articles": what the articles say is outside the text
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9087 | (2) A limited company may not purchase its own shares if as a result of the purchase there would no longer be any issued shares of the company other than redeemable shares or shares held as treasury shares.
@ref s 690(2) A limited company may not purchase its own shares if there would no longer be any issued shares other than redeemable shares or treasury shares (src:9087-9087)
GIVEN `as a result of the purchase there would no longer be any issued shares of the company other than redeemable shares or shares held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 690(2) the purchase is barred` MEANS
    IF `as a result of the purchase there would no longer be any issued shares of the company other than redeemable shares or shares held as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not purchase its own shares if as a result of the purchase there would no longer be any issued shares of the company other than redeemable shares or shares held as treasury shares"

-- ---- s 691: payment for purchase of own shares ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9089 | (1) A limited company may not purchase its own shares unless they are fully paid.
@ref s 691(1) A limited company may not purchase its own shares unless they are fully paid (src:9089-9089)
GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 691(1) the purchase is barred` MEANS
    IF `the shares are fully paid`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not purchase its own shares unless they are fully paid"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9091 | (3) But subsection (2) does not apply in a case where a private limited company is purchasing shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme.
@ref s 691(3) Subsection (2) does not apply where a private limited company is purchasing shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme (src:9091-9091)
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 691(3) subsection (2) does not apply` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private limited company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case where a private limited company is purchasing shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case where a private limited company is purchasing shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the scheme is an employees' share scheme is s 1166, answered by the caller

-- src:9090 | (2) Where a limited company purchases its own shares, the shares must be paid for on purchase.
@ref s 691(2) Where a limited company purchases its own shares, the shares must be paid for on purchase (src:9090-9090)
GIVEN `s 691(3) subsection (2) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 691(2) the shares must be paid for on purchase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 691(3) subsection (2) does not apply`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But subsection (2) does not apply in a case where a private limited company is purchasing shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (3) takes the purchase out of subsection (2) is not known

@ref s 691(2) Where a limited company purchases its own shares, the shares must be paid for on purchase (src:9090-9090)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 691(2) act in Chapter 4`
`s 691(2) the company must pay for the shares on purchase` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 691(2) pay for the shares on purchase`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 691(2): the shares were not paid for on purchase"

-- ---- s 692: financing of purchase of own shares -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9093 | (1) A private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital in accordance with Chapter 5.
@ref s 692(1) A private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital in accordance with Chapter 5 (src:9093-9093)
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(1) the private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the purchase is in accordance with Chapter 5`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with Chapter 5"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is in accordance with Chapter 5 is ss 709 to 723, answered by the caller

-- src:9097 | (1A) If the share capital of the company is not denominated in sterling, the value in sterling of the share capital shall be calculated for the purposes of subsection (1ZA)(b) at an appropriate spot rate of exchange.
@ref s 692(1A) If the share capital is not denominated in sterling, its value in sterling is calculated at an appropriate spot rate of exchange (src:9097-9097)
GIVEN `the share capital is denominated in sterling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value of the fully paid share capital in the currency in which it is denominated` IS A NUMBER
      `the spot rate of exchange, in pounds sterling for one unit of that currency` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 692(1A) the value in sterling of the share capital` MEANS
    IF `the share capital is denominated in sterling`
    THEN `the nominal value of the fully paid share capital in the currency in which it is denominated`
    ELSE `the nominal value of the fully paid share capital in the currency in which it is denominated` TIMES `the spot rate of exchange, in pounds sterling for one unit of that currency`

-- src:9098 | (1B) The rate must be a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution authorising the purchase of the shares.
@ref s 692(1B) The rate must be a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution authorising the purchase (src:9098-9098)
GIVEN `the rate is a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution authorising the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(1B) the rate is the rate the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the rate is a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution authorising the purchase`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The rate must be a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution authorising the purchase of the shares." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- s 692(1ZA): the lower of £15,000 and the nominal value of 5% of the fully paid share capital at the beginning of the financial year.
-- src:9094 | (1ZA) If authorised to do so by its articles, a private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital otherwise than in accordance with Chapter 5, up to an aggregate purchase price in a financial year of the lower of—
-- src:9095 | (a) £15,000, or
-- src:9096 | (b) the nominal value of 5% of its fully paid share capital as at the beginning of the financial year.
@ref s 692(1ZA) If authorised by its articles, a private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital up to the lower of 15,000 pounds and 5% of its fully paid share capital (src:9094-9096)
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles authorise it to purchase its own shares out of capital otherwise than in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value, in pounds sterling, of its fully paid share capital as at the beginning of the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 692(1ZA) the most the company may pay out of capital in the financial year` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If authorised to do so by its articles, a private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital"
    ELSE IF (NOT `the company's articles authorise it to purchase its own shares out of capital otherwise than in accordance with Chapter 5`)
         THEN JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If authorised to do so by its articles": no allowance otherwise
         ELSE IF 15000 AT MOST (`the nominal value, in pounds sterling, of its fully paid share capital as at the beginning of the financial year` TIMES 0.05)
              THEN JUST 15000
              ELSE JUST (`the nominal value, in pounds sterling, of its fully paid share capital as at the beginning of the financial year` TIMES 0.05)

-- src:9099 | (2) Subject to subsections (1) and (1ZA)—
-- src:9100 | (a) a limited company may only purchase its own shares out of—
-- src:9101 | (i) distributable profits of the company, or
-- src:9102 | (ii) the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase, and
-- src:9103 | (b) any premium payable on the purchase by a limited company of its own shares must be paid out of distributable profits of the company, subject to subsection (3).
@ref s 692(2) Subject to subsections (1) and (1ZA), a limited company may only purchase its own shares out of distributable profits or the proceeds of a fresh issue (src:9099-9103)
GIVEN `s 692(1) the private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the payment is within the amount s 692(1ZA) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is out of distributable profits of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(2)(a) the purchase is out of a source the section permits` MEANS
    IF (`s 692(1) the private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR `the payment is within the amount s 692(1ZA) allows`
       OR `the purchase is out of distributable profits of the company`
       OR `the purchase is out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 692(1) the private limited company may purchase its own shares out of capital` EQUALS NOTHING)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is out of capital under subsection (1) is not known, and the words "Subject to subsections (1) and (1ZA)" turn on it
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a limited company may only purchase its own shares out of— (i) distributable profits of the company, or (ii) the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase"

-- src:9104 | (3) If the shares to be purchased were issued at a premium, any premium payable on their purchase by the company may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase, up to an amount equal to—
-- src:9105 | (a) the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares purchased, or
-- src:9106 | (b) the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares),
-- src:9107 | whichever is the less.
@ref s 692(3) A premium on purchase may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue up to the lesser of the premiums received and the share premium account (src:9104-9107)
GIVEN `the shares to be purchased were issued at a premium` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares purchased` IS A NUMBER
      `the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 692(3) the most of the premium that may be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` MEANS
    IF `the shares to be purchased were issued at a premium`
    THEN IF `the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares purchased` AT MOST `the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares)`
         THEN `the aggregate of the premiums received by the company on the issue of the shares purchased`
         ELSE `the current amount of the company's share premium account (including any sum transferred to that account in respect of premiums on the new shares)`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the shares to be purchased were issued at a premium": no allowance otherwise

-- src:9099 | (2) Subject to subsections (1) and (1ZA)—
-- src:9100 | (a) a limited company may only purchase its own shares out of—
-- src:9101 | (i) distributable profits of the company, or
-- src:9102 | (ii) the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares made for the purpose of financing the purchase, and
-- src:9103 | (b) any premium payable on the purchase by a limited company of its own shares must be paid out of distributable profits of the company, subject to subsection (3).
@ref s 692(2)(b) Any premium payable on the purchase must be paid out of distributable profits, subject to subsection (3) (src:9099-9103)
GIVEN `the premium payable on the purchase` IS A NUMBER
      `the most of the premium that subsection (3) allows to be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 692(2)(b) the part of the premium that must be paid out of distributable profits` MEANS
    IF `the premium payable on the purchase` AT MOST `the most of the premium that subsection (3) allows to be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the premium payable on the purchase` MINUS `the most of the premium that subsection (3) allows to be paid out of the proceeds of a fresh issue`

-- src:9108 | (4) The amount of the company's share premium account is reduced by a sum corresponding (or by sums in the aggregate corresponding) to the amount of any payment made under subsection (3).
@ref s 692(4) The amount of the company's share premium account is reduced by a sum corresponding to any payment made under subsection (3) (src:9108-9108)
GIVEN `the amount of the company's share premium account before the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the payment made under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 692(4) the amount of the company's share premium account after the payment` MEANS
    `the amount of the company's share premium account before the payment` MINUS `the payment made under subsection (3)`

-- src:9109 | (5) This section has effect subject to section 735(4) (terms of purchase enforceable in a winding up).
@ref s 692(5) This section has effect subject to section 735(4) (terms of purchase enforceable in a winding up) (src:9109-9109)
GIVEN `s 735(4) the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 692(5) the limits of section 692 on the source of payment are displaced by section 735(4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 735(4) the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- the section has effect subject to section 735(4): where the terms may be enforced in the winding up, section 692(2) does not stop the payment (fork F-signpost)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to section 735(4)": the text displaces the section only as section 735(4) enforces the terms, and says nothing of the case where it does not
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 735(4) lets the terms be enforced is not known

-- ---- s 693: authority for purchase of own shares ----------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 693(1) kind of purchase` IS ONE OF
    `s 693(1)(a) an off-market purchase`
    `s 693(1)(b) a market purchase`

-- src:9112 | (1) A limited company may only purchase its own shares—
-- src:9113 | (a) by an off-market purchase, authorised in accordance with section 693A or in pursuance of a contract approved in advance in accordance with section 694;
-- src:9114 | (b) by a market purchase, authorised in accordance with section 701.
@ref s 693(1) A limited company may only purchase its own shares by an off-market purchase authorised under section 693A or 694, or by a market purchase authorised under section 701 (src:9112-9114)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 693(1) kind of purchase`
      `the off-market purchase is authorised in accordance with section 693A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the off-market purchase is in pursuance of a contract approved in advance in accordance with section 694` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the market purchase is authorised in accordance with section 701` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(1) the limited company may make the purchase` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 693(1)(a) an off-market purchase` THEN
         IF (`the off-market purchase is authorised in accordance with section 693A` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            OR (`the off-market purchase is in pursuance of a contract approved in advance in accordance with section 694` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (`the off-market purchase is authorised in accordance with section 693A` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                 AND (`the off-market purchase is in pursuance of a contract approved in advance in accordance with section 694` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A limited company may only purchase its own shares— (a) by an off-market purchase, authorised in accordance with section 693A or in pursuance of a contract approved in advance in accordance with section 694"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is authorised under s 693A or s 694 is not known
    WHEN `s 693(1)(b) a market purchase` THEN
         CONSIDER `the market purchase is authorised in accordance with section 701`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A limited company may only purchase its own shares— ... (b) by a market purchase, authorised in accordance with section 701"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is authorised under s 701 is not known

-- src:9118 | (3) For this purpose a company's shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on a recognised investment exchange if—
-- src:9119 | (a) they are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8), or
-- src:9120 | (b) the company has been afforded facilities for dealings in the shares to take place on the exchange—
-- src:9121 | (i) without prior permission for individual transactions from the authority governing that investment exchange, and
-- src:9122 | (ii) without limit as to the time during which those facilities are to be available.
@ref s 693(3) Shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on a recognised investment exchange if listed under Part 6 of the FSMA 2000 or the company has been afforded facilities (src:9118-9122)
GIVEN `the shares are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been afforded facilities for dealings in the shares to take place on the exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facilities are afforded without prior permission for individual transactions from the authority governing that investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facilities are afforded without limit as to the time during which they are to be available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(3) the shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange` MEANS
    IF `the shares are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
       OR (`the company has been afforded facilities for dealings in the shares to take place on the exchange`
           AND `the facilities are afforded without prior permission for individual transactions from the authority governing that investment exchange`
           AND `the facilities are afforded without limit as to the time during which they are to be available`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company's shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on a recognised investment exchange if— (a) they are listed under Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, or (b) the company has been afforded facilities ... (i) without prior permission ..., and (ii) without limit as to the time"

-- src:9115 | (2) A purchase is “off-market” if the shares either—
-- src:9116 | (a) are purchased otherwise than on a recognised investment exchange, or
-- src:9117 | (b) are purchased on a recognised investment exchange but are not subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange.
@ref s 693(2) A purchase is off-market if the shares are purchased otherwise than on a recognised investment exchange, or on one but not subject to a marketing arrangement (src:9115-9117)
GIVEN `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 693(3) the shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(2) the purchase is an off-market purchase` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are purchased on a recognised investment exchange`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 693(3) the shares are subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A purchase is “off-market” if the shares either— (a) are purchased otherwise than on a recognised investment exchange, or (b) are purchased on a recognised investment exchange but are not subject to a marketing arrangement on the exchange"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the shares are subject to a marketing arrangement is subsection (3), answered by the caller

-- src:9123 | (4) A purchase is a “market purchase” if it is made on a recognised investment exchange and is not an off-market purchase by virtue of subsection (2)(b).
@ref s 693(4) A purchase is a market purchase if it is made on a recognised investment exchange and is not an off-market purchase by virtue of subsection (2)(b) (src:9123-9123)
GIVEN `the purchase is made on a recognised investment exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 693(2) the purchase is an off-market purchase` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(4) the purchase is a market purchase` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the purchase is made on a recognised investment exchange`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A purchase is a “market purchase” if it is made on a recognised investment exchange"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 693(2) the purchase is an off-market purchase`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and is not an off-market purchase by virtue of subsection (2)(b)"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is off-market is subsection (2), answered by the caller

-- src:9124 | (5) In this section “recognised investment exchange” means a recognised investment exchange (within the meaning of Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000) other than an overseas exchange (within the meaning of that Part).
@ref s 693(5) "recognised investment exchange" means a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of Part 18 of the FSMA 2000 other than an overseas exchange (src:9124-9124)
GIVEN `the exchange is a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is an overseas exchange within the meaning of that Part` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693(5) the exchange is a recognised investment exchange` MEANS
    IF (`the exchange is an overseas exchange within the meaning of that Part` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an overseas exchange (within the meaning of that Part)"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the exchange is a recognised investment exchange within the meaning of Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“recognised investment exchange” means a recognised investment exchange (within the meaning of Part 18 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000)"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 is not among the sources
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
              CONSIDER `the exchange is an overseas exchange within the meaning of that Part`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the exchange is an overseas exchange is the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, outside the sources
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an overseas exchange (within the meaning of that Part)"

-- ---- s 693A: authority for off-market purchase for an employees' share scheme ------------------------------

-- src:9126 | (1) A company may make an off-market purchase of its own shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme if the purchase has first been authorised by a resolution of the company under this section.
@ref s 693A(1) A company may make an off-market purchase of its own shares for an employees' share scheme if the purchase has first been authorised by a resolution of the company under this section (src:9126-9126)
GIVEN `s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purchase has first been authorised by a resolution of the company under section 693A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(1) the company may make the off-market purchase` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-693A-1: "may make an off-market purchase ... if the purchase has first been authorised" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    CONSIDER `s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may make an off-market purchase of its own shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the scheme is an employees' share scheme is s 1166, answered by the caller
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `the purchase has first been authorised by a resolution of the company under section 693A`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the purchase has first been authorised by a resolution of the company under this section": the bar on an unauthorised off-market purchase is s 693(1) and s 694(1) ("only")

DECLARE `s 693A(2) form of authority` IS ONE OF
    `s 693A(2)(a) general`
    `s 693A(2)(a) limited to the purchase of shares of a particular class or description`
    `s 693A(2)(b) unconditional`
    `s 693A(2)(b) subject to conditions`
    `s 693A(2) another form`

-- src:9127 | (2) That authority—
-- src:9128 | (a) may be general or limited to the purchase of shares of a particular class or description, and
-- src:9129 | (b) may be unconditional or subject to conditions.
@ref s 693A(2) That authority may be general or limited to a class or description, and unconditional or subject to conditions (src:9127-9129)
GIVEN form IS A `s 693A(2) form of authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(2) the authority may take that form` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `s 693A(2) another form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "That authority— (a) may be general or limited to the purchase of shares of a particular class or description, and (b) may be unconditional or subject to conditions"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:9130 | (3) The authority must—
-- src:9131 | (a) specify the maximum number of shares authorised to be acquired, and
-- src:9132 | (b) determine both the maximum and minimum prices that may be paid for the shares.
@ref s 693A(3) The authority must specify the maximum number of shares and determine both the maximum and minimum prices (src:9130-9132)
GIVEN `the authority specifies the maximum number of shares authorised to be acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority determines the maximum price that may be paid for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority determines the minimum price that may be paid for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(3) the authority contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the authority specifies the maximum number of shares authorised to be acquired` AND `the authority determines the maximum price that may be paid for the shares` AND `the authority determines the minimum price that may be paid for the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authority must— (a) specify the maximum number of shares authorised to be acquired, and (b) determine both the maximum and minimum prices that may be paid for the shares." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9133 | (4) The authority may be varied, revoked or from time to time renewed by a resolution of the company.
@ref s 693A(4) The authority may be varied, revoked or from time to time renewed by a resolution of the company (src:9133-9133)
GIVEN `the authority is varied, revoked or renewed by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(4) the authority may be varied, revoked or renewed` MEANS
    IF `the authority is varied, revoked or renewed by a resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The authority may be varied, revoked or from time to time renewed by a resolution of the company"

-- src:9134 | (5) A resolution conferring, varying or renewing authority must specify a date on which it is to expire, which must not be later than five years after the date on which the resolution is passed.
@ref s 693A(5) A resolution conferring, varying or renewing authority must specify a date on which it is to expire, not later than five years after it is passed (src:9134-9134)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 693A(5) the latest date on which the authority may be specified to expire` MEANS `add years` `the date on which the resolution is passed` 5

@ref s 693A(5) A resolution conferring, varying or renewing authority must specify a date on which it is to expire, not later than five years after it is passed (src:9134-9134)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the resolution on which the authority is to expire, if it specifies one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(5) the resolution specifies a date of expiry that is not later than five years after it is passed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date specified in the resolution on which the authority is to expire, if it specifies one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify a date on which it is to expire" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
    WHEN JUST expiry THEN
         IF expiry AT MOST (`s 693A(5) the latest date on which the authority may be specified to expire` `the date on which the resolution is passed`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must not be later than five years after the date on which the resolution is passed"

-- src:9135 | (6) A company may make a purchase of its own shares after the expiry of the time limit specified if—
-- src:9136 | (a) the contract of purchase was concluded before the authority expired, and
-- src:9137 | (b) the terms of the authority permitted the company to make a contract of purchase that would or might be executed wholly or partly after its expiration.
@ref s 693A(6) A company may make a purchase after the expiry of the time limit if the contract was concluded before the authority expired and its terms permitted a contract executed after expiry (src:9135-9137)
GIVEN `the contract of purchase was concluded before the authority expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms of the authority permitted the company to make a contract of purchase that would or might be executed wholly or partly after its expiration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(6) the company may make a purchase of its own shares after the expiry of the time limit` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-693A-6: "may make a purchase ... after the expiry ... if" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    IF `the contract of purchase was concluded before the authority expired`
       AND `the terms of the authority permitted the company to make a contract of purchase that would or might be executed wholly or partly after its expiration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may make a purchase of its own shares after the expiry of the time limit specified if— (a) the contract of purchase was concluded before the authority expired, and (b) the terms of the authority permitted the company to make a contract of purchase that would or might be executed wholly or partly after its expiration"

DECLARE `s 693A(7) way of determining the price` IS ONE OF
    `s 693A(7)(a) specifying a particular sum`
    `s 693A(7)(b) providing a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion`
    `s 693A(7)(b) providing a basis or formula that refers to a person's discretion or opinion`

-- src:9138 | (7) A resolution to confer or vary authority under this section may determine the maximum or minimum price for purchase by—
-- src:9139 | (a) specifying a particular sum, or
-- src:9140 | (b) providing a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the price (but without reference to any person's discretion or opinion).
@ref s 693A(7) A resolution may determine the maximum or minimum price by specifying a sum or providing a basis or formula (without reference to any person's discretion or opinion) (src:9138-9140)
GIVEN way IS A `s 693A(7) way of determining the price`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(7) the resolution may determine the price in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 693A(7)(a) specifying a particular sum` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 693A(7)(b) providing a basis or formula for calculating the amount of the price without reference to any person's discretion or opinion` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 693A(7)(b) providing a basis or formula that refers to a person's discretion or opinion` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(but without reference to any person's discretion or opinion)"

-- src:9141 | (8) Chapter 3 of Part 3 (resolutions affecting a company's constitution) applies to a resolution under this section.
@ref s 693A(8) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to a resolution under this section (src:9141-9141)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 693A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 693A(8) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 693A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a resolution under this section"

-- ---- s 694: authority for off-market purchase -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9144 | (1) Subject to section 693A, A company may only make an off-market purchase of its own shares in pursuance of a contract approved prior to the purchase in accordance with this section.
@ref s 694(1) Subject to section 693A, a company may only make an off-market purchase in pursuance of a contract approved prior to the purchase in accordance with this section (src:9144-9144)
-- The first input is whether the purchase is authorised in accordance with s 693A: JUST TRUE where it is, JUST FALSE where the facts say it is not (not for an employees' share scheme, or not first authorised), NOTHING where that is not known.
-- A caller must not pass the NOTHING that `s 693A(1)` answers for a failed gate as if it were "not known" (see F-grant-693A-1).
GIVEN `the purchase is authorised in accordance with section 693A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is in pursuance of a contract approved prior to the purchase in accordance with section 694` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694(1) the company may make the off-market purchase` MEANS
    IF (`the purchase is authorised in accordance with section 693A` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the purchase is in pursuance of a contract approved prior to the purchase in accordance with section 694`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`the purchase is authorised in accordance with section 693A` EQUALS NOTHING)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is authorised under s 693A is not known, and the words "Subject to section 693A" turn on it
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may only make an off-market purchase of its own shares in pursuance of a contract approved prior to the purchase in accordance with this section"

-- src:9145 | (2) Either—
-- src:9146 | (a) the terms of the contract must be authorised by a . . . resolution of the company before the contract is entered into, or
-- src:9147 | (b) the contract must provide that no shares may be purchased in pursuance of the contract until its terms have been authorised by a . . . resolution of the company.
@ref s 694(2) Either the terms of the contract must be authorised by a resolution before it is entered into, or the contract must provide that no shares may be purchased until its terms are authorised (src:9145-9147)
GIVEN `the terms of the contract were authorised by a resolution of the company before the contract was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract provides that no shares may be purchased in pursuance of it until its terms have been authorised by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694(2) the contract is approved in the way the subsection requires` MEANS
    -- fork F-omitted-word: the text reads "a . . . resolution": the omitted word is not supplied, and the resolution is taken as a plain fact
    IF `the terms of the contract were authorised by a resolution of the company before the contract was entered into`
       OR `the contract provides that no shares may be purchased in pursuance of it until its terms have been authorised by a resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Either— (a) the terms of the contract must be authorised by a . . . resolution of the company before the contract is entered into, or (b) the contract must provide that no shares may be purchased in pursuance of the contract until its terms have been authorised by a . . . resolution of the company." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9148 | (3) The contract may be a contract, entered into by the company and relating to shares in the company, that does not amount to a contract to purchase the shares but under which the company may (subject to any conditions) become entitled or obliged to purchase the shares.
@ref s 694(3) The contract may be a contract that does not amount to a contract to purchase the shares but under which the company may become entitled or obliged to purchase them (src:9148-9148)
GIVEN `the contract is entered into by the company and relates to shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it amounts to a contract to purchase the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does not amount to a contract to purchase the shares but the company may (subject to any conditions) become entitled or obliged to purchase them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694(3) the contract is a contract within section 694` MEANS
    IF `the contract is entered into by the company and relates to shares in the company`
       AND (`it amounts to a contract to purchase the shares` OR `it does not amount to a contract to purchase the shares but the company may (subject to any conditions) become entitled or obliged to purchase them`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The contract may be a contract, entered into by the company and relating to shares in the company, that does not amount to a contract to purchase the shares but under which the company may (subject to any conditions) become entitled or obliged to purchase the shares"

-- src:9149 | (4) The authority conferred by a resolution under this section may be varied, revoked or from time to time renewed by a . . . resolution of the company.
@ref s 694(4) The authority may be varied, revoked or from time to time renewed by a resolution of the company (src:9149-9149)
GIVEN `the authority is varied, revoked or renewed by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694(4) the authority may be varied, revoked or renewed` MEANS
    -- fork F-omitted-word: the text reads "a . . . resolution": the omitted word is not supplied
    IF `the authority is varied, revoked or renewed by a resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The authority conferred by a resolution under this section may be varied, revoked or from time to time renewed by a . . . resolution of the company"

-- src:9150 | (5) In the case of a public company a resolution conferring, varying or renewing authority must specify a date on which the authority is to expire, which must not be later than five years after the date on which the resolution is passed.
@ref s 694(5) In the case of a public company a resolution must specify a date on which the authority is to expire, not later than five years after it is passed (src:9150-9150)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the resolution on which the authority is to expire, if it specifies one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694(5) the resolution specifies a date of expiry that is not later than five years after it is passed` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN `s 693A(5) the resolution specifies a date of expiry that is not later than five years after it is passed` `the date on which the resolution is passed` `the date specified in the resolution on which the authority is to expire, if it specifies one`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a public company a resolution conferring, varying or renewing authority must specify a date"

-- src:9151 | (6) A resolution conferring, varying, revoking or renewing authority under this section is subject to—
-- src:9152 | section 695 (exercise of voting rights), and
-- src:9153 | section 696 (disclosure of details of contract).
@ref s 694(6) A resolution conferring, varying, revoking or renewing authority is subject to sections 695 and 696 (src:9151-9153)
GIVEN `s 695(3) the resolution is not effective` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 696(5) the resolution is not validly passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 694(6) the resolution is barred by section 695 or section 696` MEANS
    IF (`s 695(3) the resolution is not effective` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 696(5) the resolution is not validly passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 695(3) the resolution is not effective` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 696(5) the resolution is not validly passed` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is subject to— section 695 (exercise of voting rights), and section 696 (disclosure of details of contract)": neither bar bites
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 695 or 696 bars the resolution is not known

-- ---- s 695: exercise of voting rights ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9155 | (1) This section applies to a resolution to confer, vary, revoke or renew authority for the purposes of section 694 (authority for off-market purchase of own shares).
@ref s 695(1) This section applies to a resolution to confer, vary, revoke or renew authority for the purposes of section 694 (src:9155-9155)
GIVEN `the resolution is one to confer, vary, revoke or renew authority for the purposes of section 694` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 695(1) this section applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is one to confer, vary, revoke or renew authority for the purposes of section 694`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a resolution to confer, vary, revoke or renew authority for the purposes of section 694"

-- src:9156 | (2) Where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, a member who holds shares to which the resolution relates is not an eligible member.
@ref s 695(2) Where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, a member who holds shares to which it relates is not an eligible member (src:9156-9156)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member holds shares to which the resolution relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 695(2) the member is not an eligible member` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` AND `the member holds shares to which the resolution relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, a member who holds shares to which the resolution relates is not an eligible member" (the subsection does not exclude him; section 289, coa7, decides)

-- src:9157 | (3) Where the resolution is proposed at a meeting of the company, it is not effective if—
-- src:9158 | (a) any member of the company holding shares to which the resolution relates exercises the voting rights carried by any of those shares in voting on the resolution, and
-- src:9159 | (b) the resolution would not have been passed if he had not done so.
@ref s 695(3) Where the resolution is proposed at a meeting, it is not effective if a member holding shares to which it relates votes and it would not have been passed without his vote (src:9157-9159)
GIVEN `the resolution is proposed at a meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the company holding shares to which the resolution relates exercises the voting rights carried by any of those shares in voting on the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution would not have been passed if he had not done so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 695(3) the resolution is not effective` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is proposed at a meeting of the company`
       AND `a member of the company holding shares to which the resolution relates exercises the voting rights carried by any of those shares in voting on the resolution`
       AND `the resolution would not have been passed if he had not done so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the resolution is proposed at a meeting of the company, it is not effective if— (a) any member ... exercises the voting rights ..., and (b) the resolution would not have been passed if he had not done so"

-- src:9161 | (a) a member who holds shares to which the resolution relates is regarded as exercising the voting rights carried by those shares not only if he votes in respect of them on a poll on the question whether the resolution shall be passed, but also if he votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll;
@ref s 695(4)(a) A member is regarded as exercising the voting rights if he votes on a poll, and also if he votes otherwise than on a poll (src:9161-9161)
GIVEN `he votes in respect of the shares on a poll on the question whether the resolution shall be passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 695(4)(a) the member is regarded as exercising the voting rights` MEANS
    IF `he votes in respect of the shares on a poll on the question whether the resolution shall be passed` OR `he votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is regarded as exercising the voting rights carried by those shares not only if he votes in respect of them on a poll ... but also if he votes on the resolution otherwise than on a poll"

-- src:9162 | (b) any member of the company may demand a poll on that question;
@ref s 695(4)(b) Any member of the company may demand a poll on that question (src:9162-9162)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 695(4)(b) the person may demand a poll on that question` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any member of the company may demand a poll on that question"

-- src:9163 | (c) a vote and a demand for a poll by a person as proxy for a member are the same respectively as a vote and a demand by the member.
@ref s 695(4)(c) A vote and a demand for a poll by a person as proxy for a member are the same as a vote and a demand by the member (src:9163-9163)
GIVEN `the vote or demand is made by a person as proxy for a member` IS A BOOLEAN
