-- src:9166 | (2) A copy of the contract (if it is in writing) or a memorandum setting out its terms (if it is not) must be made available to members—
-- src:9167 | (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
@ref s 696(2)(a) Written resolution: a copy of the contract or a memorandum is sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent (src:9166-9167)
GIVEN `the copy or memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the copy or memorandum was sent or submitted` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696(2)(a) the copy or memorandum was made available to members for a written resolution` MEANS
    IF `the copy or memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member`
       AND `the date on which the copy or memorandum was sent or submitted` AT MOST `the date on which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of the contract (if it is in writing) or a memorandum setting out its terms (if it is not) must be made available to members— (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9166 | (2) A copy of the contract (if it is in writing) or a memorandum setting out its terms (if it is not) must be made available to members—
-- src:9167 | (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
-- src:9168 | (b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both—
-- src:9169 | (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and
-- src:9170 | (ii) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 696(2)(b) Meeting: made available for inspection at the registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting and at the meeting itself (src:9166-9170)
GIVEN `the first day on which the copy or memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office, and it stayed available to the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the copy or memorandum was also available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696(2)(b) the copy or memorandum was made available to members for a resolution at a meeting` MEANS
    IF `the first day on which the copy or memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office, and it stayed available to the date of the meeting` AT MOST (`the date of the meeting` MINUS 14)
       AND `the copy or memorandum was also available for inspection at the meeting itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

@ref s 696(2) A copy of the contract or a memorandum of its terms must be made available to members (src:9166-9170)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 691(2) act in Chapter 4`
`s 696(2) the company must make the copy or memorandum available to members` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 696(2) make a copy of the contract, or a memorandum of its terms, available to members`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 696(2): a copy of the contract, or a memorandum of its terms, was not made available to members"

-- src:9171 | (3) A memorandum of contract terms so made available must include the names of the members holding shares to which the contract relates.
@ref s 696(3) A memorandum of contract terms so made available must include the names of the members holding shares to which the contract relates (src:9171-9171)
GIVEN `a memorandum of contract terms is made available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum includes the names of the members holding shares to which the contract relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696(3) the memorandum includes what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a memorandum of contract terms is made available`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A memorandum of contract terms so made available"
