@ref s 701(7) A resolution may determine either or both the maximum and minimum price by specifying a sum or providing a basis or formula (without reference to any person's discretion or opinion) (src:9226-9228)
GIVEN way IS A `s 693A(7) way of determining the price`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 701(7) the resolution may determine the price in that way` MEANS
    `s 693A(7) the resolution may determine the price in that way` way

-- src:9229 | (8) Chapter 3 of Part 3 (resolutions affecting a company's constitution) applies to a resolution under this section.
@ref s 701(8) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to a resolution under this section (src:9229-9229)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 701` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 701(8) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 701`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a resolution under this section"

-- ---- s 702: copy of contract or memorandum to be available for inspection -----------------------------------

-- src:9232 | (1) This section applies where a company has entered into—
-- src:9233 | (a) a contract approved under section 694 (authorisation of contract for off-market purchase), or
-- src:9234 | (b) a contract for a purchase authorised under section 701 (authorisation of market purchase).
@ref s 702(1) This section applies where a company has entered into a contract approved under section 694 or a contract for a purchase authorised under section 701 (src:9232-9234)
GIVEN `the company has entered into a contract approved under section 694` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has entered into a contract for a purchase authorised under section 701` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company has entered into a contract approved under section 694` OR `the company has entered into a contract for a purchase authorised under section 701`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company has entered into— (a) a contract approved under section 694 ..., or (b) a contract for a purchase authorised under section 701"

-- src:9235 | (2) The company must keep available for inspection—
-- src:9236 | (a) a copy of the contract, or
-- src:9237 | (b) if the contract is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out its terms.
@ref s 702(2) The company must keep available for inspection a copy of the contract or, if it is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out its terms (src:9235-9237)
GIVEN `s 702(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps available for inspection a copy of the contract or, if the contract is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(2) the company has kept the copy or memorandum available for inspection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 702(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company has entered into—"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `the company keeps available for inspection a copy of the contract or, if the contract is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out its terms`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must keep available for inspection— (a) a copy of the contract, or (b) if the contract is not in writing, a written memorandum setting out its terms." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

@ref s 702(2) The company must keep available for inspection a copy of the contract or a written memorandum (src:9235-9237)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 691(2) act in Chapter 4`
`s 702(2) the company must keep the copy or memorandum available for inspection` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 702(2) keep a copy of the contract, or a memorandum of its terms, available for inspection`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 702(2): the company did not keep a copy of the contract, or a memorandum of its terms, available for inspection"

-- src:9238 | (3) The copy or memorandum must be kept available for inspection from the conclusion of the contract until the end of the period of ten years beginning with—
-- src:9239 | (a) the date on which the purchase of all the shares in pursuance of the contract is completed, or
-- src:9240 | (b) the date on which the contract otherwise determines.
@ref s 702(3) The copy or memorandum must be kept available from the conclusion of the contract until the end of the period of ten years beginning with completion of the purchase or the date the contract otherwise determines (src:9238-9240)
GIVEN `the date on which the purchase of all the shares in pursuance of the contract is completed, if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the contract otherwise determines, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 702(3) the first day of the period of ten years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the purchase of all the shares in pursuance of the contract is completed, if it is`
    WHEN JUST completed THEN JUST completed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date on which the contract otherwise determines, if it does`

@ref s 702(3) The copy or memorandum must be kept available from the conclusion of the contract until the end of the period of ten years beginning with completion of the purchase or the date the contract otherwise determines (src:9238-9240)
GIVEN `the first day of the period of ten years` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 702(3) the last day of the period of ten years` MEANS (`add years` `the first day of the period of ten years` 10) MINUS 1
-- fork F-ten-years: "the end of the period of ten years beginning with" a date is read as the day before the tenth anniversary; the other reading ends on the tenth anniversary itself

@ref s 702(3) The copy or memorandum must be kept available from the conclusion of the contract until the end of the period of ten years beginning with completion of the purchase or the date the contract otherwise determines (src:9238-9240)
GIVEN `the date on which the purchase of all the shares in pursuance of the contract is completed, if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the contract otherwise determines, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 702(3) the last day on which the copy or memorandum must be kept available` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 702(3) the first day of the period of ten years` `the date on which the purchase of all the shares in pursuance of the contract is completed, if it is` `the date on which the contract otherwise determines, if it does`
    WHEN JUST first THEN JUST (`s 702(3) the last day of the period of ten years` first)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither the completion of the purchase nor the determination of the contract is known, so the period of ten years has no beginning

@ref s 702(3) The copy or memorandum must be kept available from the conclusion of the contract until the end of the period of ten years beginning with completion of the purchase or the date the contract otherwise determines (src:9238-9240)
GIVEN `it was kept available for inspection continuously from the conclusion of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day on which it was kept available for inspection` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period of ten years` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(3) the copy or memorandum was kept available for the period` MEANS
    IF `it was kept available for inspection continuously from the conclusion of the contract` AND `the last day on which it was kept available for inspection` AT LEAST `the last day of the period of ten years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy or memorandum must be kept available for inspection from the conclusion of the contract until the end of the period of ten years" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9241 | (4) The copy or memorandum must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:9242 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:9243 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 702(4) The copy or memorandum must be kept available at the registered office or at a place specified in regulations under section 1136 (src:9241-9243)
GIVEN `it is kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(4) the copy or memorandum is kept at a place the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `it is kept at the company's registered office` OR `it is kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy or memorandum must be kept available for inspection— (a) at the company's registered office, or (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9244 | (5) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:9245 | (a) of the place at which the copy or memorandum is kept available for inspection, and
-- src:9246 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:9247 | unless it has at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 702(5) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change, unless it has at all times been kept at the registered office (src:9244-9247)
GIVEN `it has at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(5) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place` MEANS
    IF `it has at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it has at all times been kept at the company's registered office"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The text states no period for the notice of s 702(5): the 14 days appear only in s 703(1), as the default that makes an offence.
@ref s 702(5) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change (src:9244-9247)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 691(2) act in Chapter 4`
`s 702(5) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar of the place` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 702(5) give notice to the registrar of the place at which the copy or memorandum is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 702(5): the company did not give notice to the registrar of the place at which the copy or memorandum is kept"

DECLARE `s 702(6) who inspects` IS ONE OF
    `s 702(6)(a) a member of the company`
    `s 702(6)(b) any other person`

-- src:9248 | (6) Every copy or memorandum required to be kept under this section must be kept open to inspection without charge—
-- src:9249 | (a) by any member of the company, and
-- src:9250 | (b) in the case of a public company, by any other person.
@ref s 702(6) The copy or memorandum must be open to inspection without charge by any member and, in the case of a public company, by any other person (src:9248-9250)
GIVEN who IS A `s 702(6) who inspects`
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(6) the person may inspect the copy or memorandum without charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `s 702(6)(a) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 702(6)(b) any other person` THEN
         IF `the company is a public company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of a public company, by any other person"

-- src:9251 | (7) The provisions of this section apply to a variation of a contract as they apply to the original contract.
@ref s 702(7) The provisions of this section apply to a variation of a contract as they apply to the original contract (src:9251-9251)
GIVEN `the document is the copy or memorandum of a variation of a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 702(7) section 702 applies to the document as it applies to the original contract` MEANS
    IF `the document is the copy or memorandum of a variation of a contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to a variation of a contract"

-- ---- s 703: enforcement of right to inspect copy or memorandum ------------------------------------------------

-- src:9253 | (1) If default is made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4) or default is made for 14 days in complying with section 702(5), or an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9254 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9255 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 703(1) Default in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4), default for 14 days in complying with section 702(5), or a refusal of an inspection required under section 702(6) (src:9253-9255)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with section 702(5)` IS A NUMBER
      `an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 703(1) the company is in default as the subsection describes` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4)`
       OR `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with section 702(5)` AT LEAST 14
       OR `an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4) or default is made for 14 days in complying with section 702(5), or an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused"

-- src:9253 | (1) If default is made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4) or default is made for 14 days in complying with section 702(5), or an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9254 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9255 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 703(1) Offence (src:9253-9255)
GIVEN `the company is in default as section 703(1) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 703(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company is in default as section 703(1) describes`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with section 702(2), (3) or (4) or default is made for 14 days in complying with section 702(5), or an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:9256 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 703(2) Penalty (src:9256-9256)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 703(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states the penalty on summary conviction only
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF how, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- src:9257 | (3) In the case of refusal of an inspection required under section 702(6) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection.
@ref s 703(3) In the case of refusal of an inspection required under section 702(6) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection (src:9257-9257)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 703(3) the court may order an immediate inspection` MEANS
    IF `an inspection required under section 702(6) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of refusal of an inspection required under section 702(6) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection"

-- ---- s 704: no assignment of company's right to purchase own shares -------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 704 the section under which the contract is authorised` IS ONE OF
    `s 704(za) section 693A`
    `s 704(a) section 694`
    `s 704(b) section 701`
    `s 704 none of those sections`

-- src:9259 | The rights of a company under a contract authorised under—
-- src:9260 | (za) section 693A (authority for off-market purchase for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme),
-- src:9261 | (a) section 694 (authority for off-market purchase), or
-- src:9262 | (b) section 701 (authority for market purchase)
-- src:9263 | are not capable of being assigned.
@ref s 704 The rights of a company under a contract authorised under section 693A, 694 or 701 are not capable of being assigned (src:9259-9263)
GIVEN authority IS A `s 704 the section under which the contract is authorised`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 704 the company's right under the contract is capable of being assigned` MEANS
    CONSIDER authority
    WHEN `s 704 none of those sections` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The rights of a company under a contract authorised under— (za) section 693A ..., (a) section 694 ..., or (b) section 701"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not capable of being assigned"

-- ---- s 705: payments apart from purchase price to be made out of distributable profits ---------------------------

DECLARE `s 705(1) what the payment is in consideration of` IS ONE OF
    `s 705(1)(a) acquiring a right with respect to the purchase of its own shares in pursuance of a contingent purchase contract approved under section 694`
    `s 705(1)(b) the variation of a contract approved under section 694`
    `s 705(1)(c) the release of an obligation of the company with respect to the purchase of its own shares under a contract approved under section 694 or authorised under section 701`
    `s 705(1) something else`

-- src:9265 | (1) A payment made by a company in consideration of—
-- src:9266 | (a) acquiring any right with respect to the purchase of its own shares in pursuance of a contingent purchase contract approved under section 694 (authorisation of off-market purchase),
-- src:9267 | (b) the variation of any contract approved under that section, or
-- src:9268 | (c) the release of any of the company's obligations with respect to the purchase of any of its own shares under a contract—
-- src:9269 | (i) approved under section 694, or
-- src:9270 | (ii) authorised under section 701 (authorisation of market purchase),
-- src:9271 | must be made out of the company's distributable profits.
@ref s 705(1) A payment in consideration of acquiring a right, a variation or a release must be made out of the company's distributable profits (src:9265-9271)
GIVEN consideration IS A `s 705(1) what the payment is in consideration of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 705(1) the payment must be made out of the company's distributable profits` MEANS
    CONSIDER consideration
    WHEN `s 705(1) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A payment made by a company in consideration of— (a) ..., (b) ..., or (c) ..."
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 705(2) consequence of the requirement not being met` IS ONE OF
    `s 705(2)(a) no purchase by the company of its own shares in pursuance of that contract may be made under Chapter 4`
    `s 705(2)(b) no purchase following the variation may be made under Chapter 4`
    `s 705(2)(c) the purported release is void`
    `s 705(2) no consequence under this subsection`

-- src:9272 | (2) If this requirement is not met in relation to a contract, then—
-- src:9273 | (a) in a case within subsection (1)(a), no purchase by the company of its own shares in pursuance of that contract may be made under this Chapter;
-- src:9274 | (b) in a case within subsection (1)(b), no such purchase following the variation may be made under this Chapter;
-- src:9275 | (c) in a case within subsection (1)(c), the purported release is void.
@ref s 705(2) If the requirement is not met, no purchase may be made under the contract, or following the variation, and a purported release is void (src:9272-9275)
GIVEN consideration IS A `s 705(1) what the payment is in consideration of`
      `the requirement that the payment be made out of distributable profits is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 705(2) consequence of the requirement not being met`
`s 705(2) the consequence of the requirement not being met` MEANS
    IF `the requirement that the payment be made out of distributable profits is met`
    THEN `s 705(2) no consequence under this subsection` -- the consequences follow "If this requirement is not met"
    ELSE CONSIDER consideration
         WHEN `s 705(1)(a) acquiring a right with respect to the purchase of its own shares in pursuance of a contingent purchase contract approved under section 694` THEN `s 705(2)(a) no purchase by the company of its own shares in pursuance of that contract may be made under Chapter 4`
         WHEN `s 705(1)(b) the variation of a contract approved under section 694` THEN `s 705(2)(b) no purchase following the variation may be made under Chapter 4`
         WHEN `s 705(1)(c) the release of an obligation of the company with respect to the purchase of its own shares under a contract approved under section 694 or authorised under section 701` THEN `s 705(2)(c) the purported release is void`
         WHEN `s 705(1) something else` THEN `s 705(2) no consequence under this subsection`

-- ---- s 706: treatment of shares purchased ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9277 | Where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with this Chapter, then—
-- src:9278 | (a) if section 724 (treasury shares) applies, the shares may be held and dealt with in accordance with Chapter 6;
@ref s 706(a) Where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with this Chapter, if section 724 applies the shares may be held and dealt with in accordance with Chapter 6 (src:9277-9278)
GIVEN `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 706(a) the shares may be held and dealt with in accordance with Chapter 6` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with this Chapter, then"
    ELSE `s 724(1) this section applies` TRUE `the purchase is made out of distributable profits`

-- src:9277 | Where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with this Chapter, then—
-- src:9278 | (a) if section 724 (treasury shares) applies, the shares may be held and dealt with in accordance with Chapter 6;
-- src:9279 | (b) if that section does not apply—
-- src:9280 | (i) the shares are treated as cancelled, and
@ref s 706(b)(i) If section 724 does not apply, the shares are treated as cancelled (src:9277-9280)
GIVEN `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 706(b)(i) the shares are treated as cancelled` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with this Chapter, then"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 724(1) this section applies` TRUE `the purchase is made out of distributable profits`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if that section does not apply"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:9277 | Where a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with this Chapter, then—
-- src:9278 | (a) if section 724 (treasury shares) applies, the shares may be held and dealt with in accordance with Chapter 6;
-- src:9279 | (b) if that section does not apply—
-- src:9280 | (i) the shares are treated as cancelled, and
-- src:9281 | (ii) the amount of the company's issued share capital is diminished accordingly by the nominal value of the shares cancelled.
@ref s 706(b)(ii) If section 724 does not apply, the issued share capital is diminished by the nominal value of the shares cancelled (src:9277-9281)
GIVEN `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is made out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the company's issued share capital before the purchase` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the shares cancelled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 706(b)(ii) the amount of the company's issued share capital after the purchase` MEANS
    IF `a limited company makes a purchase of its own shares in accordance with Chapter 4` AND (`s 724(1) this section applies` TRUE `the purchase is made out of distributable profits`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN `the amount of the company's issued share capital before the purchase` MINUS `the nominal value of the shares cancelled`
    ELSE `the amount of the company's issued share capital before the purchase` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if that section does not apply— (ii) the amount of the company's issued share capital is diminished accordingly"

-- ---- s 707: return to registrar of purchase of own shares ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9283 | (1) Where a company purchases shares under this Chapter, it must deliver a return to the registrar within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the shares are delivered to it.
@ref s 707(1) Where a company purchases shares under this Chapter, it must deliver a return to the registrar within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the shares are delivered to it (src:9283-9283)
GIVEN `the date on which the shares are delivered to the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 707(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` MEANS `the date on which the shares are delivered to the company` PLUS 27

@ref s 707(1) Where a company purchases shares under this Chapter, it must deliver a return to the registrar within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the shares are delivered to it (src:9283-9283)
GIVEN `the date on which the shares are delivered to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company delivered the return to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 707(1) the return was delivered within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the shares were delivered` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company delivered the return to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the shares are delivered to the company`
       AND `the date on which the company delivered the return to the registrar` AT MOST (`s 707(1) the last day for delivering the return to the registrar` `the date on which the shares are delivered to the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must deliver a return to the registrar within the period of 28 days beginning with the date on which the shares are delivered to it"

